WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.650
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:04.860
happening all the time,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.880
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.080
from August to test for ourselves.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.220
These Chameleon Flakes
from Kaima Cosmetics

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.820
have been everywhere lately.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.130
They're definitely a unique product,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.650
because they're like
little shavings of pigment

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.980
that shift color.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.280
I wanted to try these mixed with

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.470
the Glistening Pigment Mix,

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.255
which is how I saw it
being used all over TikTok,

00:00:24.255 --> 00:00:26.813
but I could not get this to look good

00:00:26.813 --> 00:00:27.938
no matter what I did --

00:00:27.938 --> 00:00:30.232
adding more of the mix, using less,

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:31.398
mixing it for longer.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.223
It honestly doesn't
look that bad on camera,

00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:34.533
but nothing was making it look

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:37.130
like what I saw in so many videos.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.410
I finally decided to use
it how it's recommended

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.440
on the product page:

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.440
just apply a thin layer
of glitter adhesive

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.531
and tap the flakes on,

00:00:43.531 --> 00:00:45.310
and it worked amazingly.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.260
These look so beautiful on the eyes,

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.243
they really do,

00:00:48.243 --> 00:00:50.610
but they come with a
bit of a learning curve.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.820
I am so into no-makeup makeup right now,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.700
and I had to try out
L'Oréal's new tinted serum

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.310
with hyaluronic acid.

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.440
I'm usually very skeptical of products

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.760
that combine skin care and makeup,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.340
but I'm a huge fan of this.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.398
The coverage is light

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:06.665
but does a great job
of evening the skin out

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.410
and giving a very glowy, hydrated finish,

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.490
and it claims to smooth
your skin over time.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.640
I don't know how true that is,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.477
but if you're looking for

00:01:14.477 --> 00:01:16.251
a great skin tint at the drugstore,

00:01:16.251 --> 00:01:18.320
this is one of the best I've ever tried.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.320
Coley Cosmetics is a new brand for me.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.860
These eye-shadow bases
were all over social media,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.230
and I was very intrigued

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.370
because I've never used
a colored base before.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.820
So to see what the difference was,

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.570
I applied the base to just one eye

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.650
and then applied shadow to both eyes.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.010
This shadow is super pigmented on its own,

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.903
but I could immediately see the difference

00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:39.370
in the eye with the base versus without.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.678
The color was more pigmented, vibrant,

00:01:41.678 --> 00:01:43.420
it even felt more neon to me,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.540
and I didn't use that much,

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.300
so I was super impressed with this.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:47.283
Even the inner corner

00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:49.324
on the eye with the base was brighter.

00:01:49.324 --> 00:01:51.180
They sell every color you'll ever need,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.008
and you get so much product for $14.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.783
Next, I tried these little
cotton-swab lipsticks

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.090
from Fomomy.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:01.023
You basically snap its neck,

00:02:01.023 --> 00:02:03.039
and the lipstick inside the stick

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:06.320
drains to the bottom
end, and then you apply.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.995
This ... worked.

00:02:07.995 --> 00:02:10.180
I mean, I can't say that it didn't work.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.746
The actual lipstick itself

00:02:11.746 --> 00:02:14.671
feels like a very thin liquid.

00:02:14.671 --> 00:02:16.620
Once it dries, it really doesn't budge,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.430
and it lasted on me all day.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.790
The color was definitely there,

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.569
but the stain looked patchy

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:23.980
because I had some dry patches on my lips.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.163
I don't really see the point

00:02:26.163 --> 00:02:27.346
in a product like this.

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:30.250
Maybe if you're always
on the go or something,

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.908
or if applying regular lipstick

00:02:31.908 --> 00:02:33.683
has just gotten too boring for you,

00:02:33.683 --> 00:02:36.140
but this seems like a lot of waste

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.200
for just an OK lip stain.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.090
It was fun to snap them open, though.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.090
And, finally, we have
an interesting product

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:46.110
from Pat McGrath, the
IntensifEyes Artistry Wand.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:49.320
I was confused as to
what this was at first,

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.600
because it just looks like
a fancy $32 Chapstick,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.310
but it's essentially a mixing liquid

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:59.180
in a convenient pen form
that intensifies eye shadow.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.720
So I applied it to just one eye

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.350
to see what the difference would be.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:04.060
To make things even more difficult,

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.410
I used a patchy eye shadow from E.l.f.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.210
and also one of my dustiest,
crustiest shimmers.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.010
This shimmer is literally four years old

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.120
and pretty dried out,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.070
but I have to say that this stuff

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.120
did make these shadows look more vibrant

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.070
and surprisingly easy to blend

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.240
without getting patchy.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.980
Look at how different these eyes look.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.990
It mainly seems like one of those products

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.690
that's made for a makeup-artist kit

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.393
and not an everyday consumer.

